content.text:
Interesting: seed 4407 final prey 66 with 240 gens, previoustrace at 240 was 173 because default config changed (regrowth now 6% per gen = same 0.5%/tick; initial config? Yes default predator count and repro threshold same as H; trace final 173 at seed 4407. Why now 66? In trace we set initial predator 12, H exact; but here default `SPECIES.predator.initCount=12`, baseCost default .08 etc, yes. Differences: `mutation` default? 8. `regrowth` trace .5% per tick = 6% per gen. We changed vision effects—now during bloom, prey can't see predators and predators can't find prey. That changes dynamics significantly. Also we changed initial prey max? no. In the sim defaults, predator `init` etc. Did we miss `energyDensity` etc? yes set. Why final 66 vs 173 at 300? Note trace ran 240 and final 173; now 240 final 66. Big difference due to vision effect (bloom starts at 230, lasts 16; during bloom prey vision ~45%, could crash; trace bloom at 230 without vision effect, final 173; now 66). Seed 7 max prey 1529 near cap 1600. All runs still survive. Default seed 4407 final low-ish 66 prey, 26 predator—still alive, interesting story. At 300 it might recover. Fine. But for a default run, ending at very low prey populations is dramatic; dashboard shows a crash. The record will be interesting. However the final bloom tint may still be active at 240; dashboard charts can show it. Good.

Yet I worry about extinction risk: with bloom reducing vision, prey may starve; seed 4407 final 66 but 26 predators. They can rebound after bloom ends. Run horizon 240 stops during the bloom (started 230, ends 246). The scenario ends mid-calamity. That's okay and dramatic.

Need to verify UI performance and start coding. But also ecological logic: with `_plantProbe` signature changed, ensure no leftover references. Run passes. Good.

Catastrophe intervals default 55, 85, 115 -> within 240 have 8 events (drought 55,110,165,220; plague 85,170; bloom 115,230). That's quite frequent and overlapping. The ledger has 8 events. Good. For a 240-gen run, events at every ~55 gen. The interval controls can change. 

Maybe initial default horizon should be 200 rather than 240? The user's request mentions N generations; choice is ours. 240 with default speed 2× -> ~48s. Good. Events dramatic. 

Now build the UI. This is the major effort. Let me write the HTML/CSS first with placeholders for JS. Maybe write the entire file in sections using write, then edit. It's going to be long (maybe 2500 lines). I need to be careful with syntax.

Plan file sections:
1. Head meta, favicon, style.
2. SVG defs.
3. App markup.
4. Record overlay markup.
5. Script: sim core (paste final sim.js but without module export; as IIFE returning object). Then UI code.

I'll embed the entire sim code with the CSS/UI. To avoid drift, after assembling, I can extract the sim code and run tests on index.html with a script that evals the extracted core. Or simply copy DEV sim.js at the point of assembly and run tests via extraction. I'll do that.

Let me design the CSS in thorough detail now, then markup.

### Detailed CSS

Fonts:
```css
--serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", "Book Antiqua", Palatino, "Times New Roman", Georgia, serif;
--mono: "SFMono-Regular", "SFMono-Medium", Menlo, "Cascadia Mono", "Roboto Mono", Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
```
Iowan Old Style supports old-style figures; use `font-feature-settings: "onum" 1, "kern" 1, "liga" 1;` for display? For data use tabular. Better use `"lnum" 1, "tnum" 1` for numbers in mono. The title can have small caps: use uppercase + tracking rather than font-variant.

Base:
```css
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html,body { margin:0; padding:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--bone); }
html { -webkit-text-size-adjust:100%; }
body { font-family:var(--serif); min-height:100dvh; overflow-x:hidden; }
body.record-open { overflow:hidden; }
::selection { background: rgba(199,161,95,.3); color:#fff; }
button, input { font: inherit; color: inherit; }
button { cursor:pointer; background:none; border:none; }
```
Atmosphere:
```css
.ambient { position:fixed; inset:0; pointer-events:none; z-index:0;
 background:
  radial-gradient(90rem 60rem at 18% -10%, rgba(176,150,95,.075), transparent 55%),
  radial-gradient(70rem 50rem at 105% 110%, rgba(99,132,104,.06), transparent 60%),
  linear-gradient(180deg,#0a0d0a 0%, #080a08 60%, #090b09 100%);
}
.ambient::before { content:""; position:absolute; inset:0; opacity:.35; background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, transparent 0 2px, rgba(255,255,255,.008) 2px 3px); } // CRT? maybe too tech. Naturalist no.
.grain { position:fixed; inset:0; z-index:1; pointer-events:none; opacity:.055; background-image:url("data:image/svg+xml,..."); mix-blend-mode:screen; }
.page-frame { position:fixed; inset:12px; border:1px solid rgba(226,216,192,.10); z-index:2; pointer-events:none; }
.page-frame::before/after corner marks ... 
```
Use a double frame at larger screens. Need not interfere.

Content wrapper:
```css
.folio { position:relative; z-index:3; min-height:100dvh; display:flex; flex-direction:column; }
.masthead { display:flex; align-items:flex-end; justify-content:space-between; gap:24px; padding: clamp(18px,2.4vh,28px) clamp(24px,3.4vw,52px) 16px; }
.brand ... 
.wordmark { font-size: clamp(22px,2vw,29px); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:.17em; text-transform:uppercase; margin:0; line-height:1; }
.wordmark .no { font-family:var(--serif); font-style:italic; text-transform:none; letter-spacing:.02em; color:var(--brass-bright); font-size:.6em; margin-left:.7em; }
.subtitle { margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; font-style:italic; letter-spacing:.035em; color:var(--muted); }
.wordmark::first-letter? no.
```
Maybe add a tiny rule with a diamond after title. Use `.brand-rule`.

Masthead meta:
```css
.masthead-meta { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:26px; }
.meta-item { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:4px; }
.meta-label { font:9px var(--mono); letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--faint); }
.meta-value { font:11px var(--mono); color:var(--bone-dim); letter-spacing:.04em; }
.status-live { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; font:10px var(--mono); letter-spacing:.14em; color:var(--plant); }
.status-dot { width:5px; height:5px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--plant); box-shadow:0 0 0 3px rgba(159,190,122,.09); animation:pulse 3.2s ease-in-out infinite; }
drawer-toggle: a bordered button with a small chevron icon. On mobile hides.
```
Header bottom double rule:
```css
.masthead { border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-soft); }
.masthead::after? use .top-rule div with display flex + diamond; 
.rule { height:1px; margin:0 clamp(24px,3.4vw,52px); background:var(--line-soft); position:relative; }
.rule::before { content:""; position:absolute; left:0; right:0; top:3px; height:1px; background:rgba(...,.04); }
