Now write UI JS. This is large. Let's outline thoroughly before writing.

### UI JS detailed implementation

Top:
```js
(() => {
  'use strict';
  const SIM = VIVARIUM_SIM;
  const $ = (sel, root = document) => root.querySelector(sel);
  const $$ = ...
  const REDUCED = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  const BASE_TPS = 30;
  const clamp = ...
  const pad = ...
  const fmtInt = n => n.toLocaleString('en-US');
  const fmtTime = s => ...
  const TAU = Math.PI*2;
  const eventDefs = SIM.EVENT_DEFS;
  const genTicks = SIM.TICKS_PER_GEN;
  const DEFAULT_SPEED = 2;
  const speedToSlider = speed => Math.log(speed/0.25)/Math.log(32)*100;
  const sliderToSpeed = t => 0.25 * Math.pow(32, t/100);
```
Note: use `Math.log(8)` etc.

Elements object:
```js
const els = {
  folio, statusChip, statusText, ... all IDs
};
```
I will reference with $ directly where convenient but a map is cleaner.

State:
```js
const state = {
  world: null,
  speed: 2,
  running: true,
  finished: false,
  headless: false,
  record: null,
  recordOpen: false,
  lastFrame: 0,
  accumulator: 0,
  lastUi: 0,
  lastDial: 0,
  lastChrono: 0,
  hovered: null, // agent
  hoverUid: null,
  pointer: { inside:false, x:0, y:0, px:0, py:0 },
  announced: new Set(),
  activeTypes: new Set(),
  bannerTimer: 0,
  recordTimer: 0,
  seedFlashTimer...
  configValue...
  visualMotes: [],
  chartCanvases: [],
  tooltipEl: null,
  startedAt: performance.now(),
  lastCounts: {..},
  lastNote: '',
  lastCondition: '',
  wasRunning: true,
  recordTrigger: null,
  returnFocus: null,
};
```
We'll use `let world` instead of state.world for easier access. But API getter needs current. Use `let world = null;`.

`DEFAULTS`: config values from inputs. 
```js
function configFromControls() {
  return {
    seed: clampInt(els.seedInput.value, 1, 9999),
    mutation: parseFloat(els.mutationRange.value),
    regrowth: parseFloat(els.regrowthRange.value),
    generations: clampInt(els.horizonInput.value, 40, 2000),
    catastrophes: {
      drought:{interval: clampInt(els.droughtInput.value,15,400), armed: toggleState.drought},
      ...
    }
  };
}
```
Toggle state stored on buttons via aria-checked. On config read, query.

Control initialization:
- Set slider CSS var based on value and min/max: `applyRangeVisual(input)`.
- set initial values from markup / defaults. For tempo raw 60.
- Add event listeners.

World creation:
```js
function createRun({seed, keepRecordFocus}) {
  hideRecord(true);
  clearTimeout(state.recordTimer);
  const cfg = configFromControls();
  // update seed footer, totals, ranges etc.
  state.config = cfg;
  world = new SIM.World(cfg);
  state.running = true;
  state.finished = false;
  state.headless = false;
  state.accumulator = 0;
  state.lastFrame = performance.now();
  state.announced.clear();
  state.activeTypes.clear();
  state.startedAt = performance.now();
  state.record = null;
  hideHeadless();
  clearBanner(true);
  setTint(null);
  set condition clear;
  resetHoldUI();
  makeMotes(cfg.seed);
  update all icons/labels; updateFields? target from world.
  updateStatsNow();
  drawAllSparks(); updateDialLabels();
  // render once
}
```
- When called from seed changes, update UI controls? The controls already contain the seed. When called from new seed, set input.
- Set `els.chronoEnd.textContent = world.target`, genTotal, horizon aside.
- On recast, reset `els.seedInput.value`? Keep.
- Running auto. If document hidden? not relevant.
- Hide record if open.
- `updateTransport()`.
- `requestAnimationFrame` loop is already running from init. On initial load, createRun.
- If a previous autoRecord timer exists, clear.

UI updates:
```js
function tickUI(now, force=false) {
  if (!force && now - state.lastUi < 100) return;
  state.lastUi = now;
  const s = world.snapshot()? snapshot allocates objects/JSON every 100ms -> excessive. Don't use snapshot. Read directly:
  gen, target, counts, cover, nextEvent() (allocates small).
  update texts.
  detectEvents(now);
  updateFieldNote();
  updateTransport...
  update seed footer maybe only on seed changes.
  update condition / counts.
  update dial short counts (every UI update; okay).
  update chrono summary maybe at event changes.
}
```
Counts: `world.prey.length`, `world.predators.length`; cover.
- Update `els.genNow` with pad; target; genFill width.
- `els.floraValue.textContent = Math.round(cover*100);` prey/pred counts with commas.
- `els.footerGen.textContent = pad`.
- Detect when world.done → `finishRun('horizon')`; main loop also does. Only once.
- condition: determine active types. If active, choose newest event; set `data-event`, text e.g. event name uppercase. If multiple, show `DROUGHT + BLOOM`? Use primary, and a small count indicator maybe `"DROUGHT +1"`. To keep within space, join with " + " if two; if three "3 CALAMITIES". Implement:
  - `const names = activeEvents.map(e => eventDefs[e.type].name.toUpperCase());`
  - if 0: CLEAR
  - if 1: names[0]
  - if 2: names[0]+" + "+names[1]
  - if 3: "FULL CALAMITY" maybe too dramatic; "THREE WINDS". Better just "DROUGHT +2". Keep simple: join with " + " (will fit? DROUGHT + PLAGUE is 17 chars; condition chip maybe wide but fine). Use max 2; third "+1". 
  - data-event = newest type; colors the chip.
- Banner and tints via event detection:
  - Compare current active event keys to `state.activeTypes`.
  - For each active event not in previous, announce; for each ended announce lift? Add a live message. We show banner for new. Maintain a set of announced events by `${type}:${start}` to avoid repeating. `world.events` includes all, but active events list only. Use `state.announced`.
  - For an event in active with key not in announced: record and show. If multiple new, show the last.
  - When no active event but previous had, set tint null and update condition. Maybe announce lifts for each ended: need know which ended. Compare previous map; store `state.activeKeys` = Set of type:start. For ended, get type from key; announce "The X lifts." Only if not finished; if new event starts simultaneously, maybe skip lift announcement to avoid noise. Implement modest.
  - Tint: newest active event type. Set CSS class/data attribute. If none, remove active. Add `.tint` background using JS generated gradient? CSS classes based on data attribute, as planned. Need CSS for `.tint[data-event=...]` not yet included! I included generic tint but no event-specific backgrounds. Add now in CSS via update later. I'll handle.
  - Banner copy: fill from eventDefs; class show; clear state; set timer to hide after 4.2s. If the event ends before, hide? The banner auto-hides. Fine.
  - Live region text.
  - Update condition immediately.
  - Add `.is-active` to calamity items; `.is-off` class on off.
  - `chronoSummary` update only on events changes.
- Field note: compute only when world gen or active types change. Provide notes; use italic. Need not update every 100ms but okay.
- Estimate: update every 500ms.
- Any DOM text change can cause layout, but tiny.

`detectEvents` also update tints and CSS `--ev`? The banner's style property.

`showBanner(type, ev)`:
```js
els.banner.style.setProperty('--ev-color', def.color);
els.calamityRoman.textContent = def.num;
...
els.banner.classList.add('is-showing');
clearTimeout(...); state.bannerTimer=setTimeout(()=> el.classList.remove('is-showing'), 4200);
```
- Also maybe update `document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--event-color', def.color)`? Not needed.
- The tint:
  - set `els.tint.dataset.event = type` and add `.is-active`. For overlapping, maybe use data-event of latest; CSS uses background. Add a second ghost layer? We can create a CSS custom property `--tint-color` and style `background: radial-gradient(...var(--tint-color)...)`. Use rgba? Can't use hex alpha easily; use `color-mix` or set full value in JS. Use JS:
```js
const def = EVENT_DEFS[type];
els.tint.style.background = `radial-gradient(120% 100% at 50% 0%, ${hexToRgba(def.color, .18)}, transparent 60%), linear-gradient(180deg, ${hexToRgba(def.color,.05)}, transparent 45%)`;
els.tint.classList.add('is-active');
```
- If overlapping events, generate multiple radial gradients with each color:
```js
const layers = active.map(e => `radial-gradient(110% 90% at 50% ${15+...}%, ${hexToRgba(color,.14)}, transparent 62%)`).join(',');
```
Nice. When none, remove active. Use transition opacity. Good.
- Condition data-event from newest event.
- For ending, if no active: tint fades; condition resets.
- Banner maybe also when a manually triggered event via API. The UI polls and sees it.

Field note logic:
```js
function noteFor(world) {
 const active = world.activeEvents;
 if (active.length) return EVENT_DEFS[active[active.length-1].type].note + '.';
 const pc=world.prey.length, dc=world.predators.length, flora=world.cover*100;
 if (world.done) return 'The glass is sealed. The record has begun.';
 if (pc===0) return 'The moths are gone; the moss closes over their grazing lines.';
 if (dc===0) return 'No shrikes remain. The moths multiply in the quiet.';
 if (flora<8) return 'Grazed to the quick; the glass shows through the green.';
 if (pc>700) return 'The moths crowd the light; every frond is spoken for.';
 if (dc > Math.max(2, pc*0.18)) return 'The shrikes press close. The moths move in nervous arcs.';
 if (flora>92) return 'The meadow is unbroken; the glass has gone green.';
 const notes = ['A quiet generation. The glass keeps its counsel.','Small inheritances accumulate at the grazing line.','The shrikes quarter the field, patient as a held breath.','The moss closes behind the moths, unhurried.'];
 return notes[Math.floor(world.gen/17) % notes.length];
}
```
Don't end every with a period if source note doesn't; use proper. Field notes are italic. Use a period. Avoid overwriting too fast—when condition active, use its note. Good.

- On paused, add "held" stamp; update status and `heldText`.
- `updateTransportState()`: if finished: hold disabled, step disabled, sealLabel = "Record", seal icon maybe; recast active, headless disabled; status sealed; condition? Clear. Set class `.is-held` etc. If paused: status HELD, hold label RESUME/play icon. If running: LIVE/pause. Also the aria-label of hold.
